  "reason": "Evidence: scVI n200 (config_004, acc 0.5203) outperforms PCA n2000 (config_001, acc 0.4849) as the RNA encoder, and image-only models are weak (config_010, acc 0.2079). The most important untested design axis is whether multiprofile aggregation adds value over singleprofile. Question: Does switching from singleprofile to multiprofile (with the simplest aggregation, avgpool) improve accuracy when paired with the best RNA encoder identified so far (scVI n200)? This is the minimal-change extension of our best result (config_004 → config_005), isolating the profile-setting effect while holding the encoder fixed. If multiprofile+avgpool helps, the next experiment can test transformer aggregation (config_006); if it doesn't, we avoid wasting budget on a more complex aggregation that is unlikely to rescue a weak profile setting. With 6 experiments remaining, establishing whether multiprofile is beneficial is the highest-priority uncertainty to resolve before investing in multimodal fusion experiments."
}

